---
title = "Escape HTML"
meta_title = "How to escape HTML in Gleam"
subtitle = "using Houdini"
description = "The Houdini package provides HTML escaping that works with Gleam on both Erlang and JavaScript"
tags = ["html", "security"]
---

The `houdini` package provides fast HTML escaping that work on both the
Erlang and JavaScript targets. Add it as a dependency to your package:

```cli
gleam add houdini
```

Use the [`houdini.escape`](https://houdini.hexdocs.pm/houdini.html#escape)
to escape HTML content.

```gleam
import houdini

pub fn render_paragraph(content: String) -> String {
  let content = houdini.escape(content)
  "<p>" <> content <> "</p>"
}
```

Content escaped with `houdini.escape` is safe to include in a HTML page, even
if the content comes from an untrusted source, such as user input.
